 # Config Surface
 
+The optional `tokenSaver` object in `src/config/schema/config-schema.ts` is disabled when
+absent. Its strict protocol-v1 configuration accepts only the fixed local transform origin.
+It does not configure a provider. See the [prototype contract](transports/responses.md#token-saver-prototype).
+
+`src/config/token-saver-control.ts` exposes only this subtree through
+`ocx config token-saver-state --json` and
+`ocx config token-saver-set <expected-sha256> <json-or-null> --json`.
+The fingerprint hashes UTF-8 JSON of [protocol, enabled, endpoint, tokenFile], or null.
+Writes recheck that fingerprint inside the existing persisted-config transaction on every
+rebase; stale callers cannot overwrite an external extension edit. Provider credentials
+are neither returned nor changed. Protocol v1 requires an absolute token path.
+
+The serving process adds `tokenSaver: { protocol: 1, control: 1, enabled: boolean }`
+to readyz. Existing PID/port checks validate the process; `ocx ready --json` forwards
+only those typed fields on success. Readiness and each outbound dispatch resolve the
+persisted extension policy, so CLI controls take effect without restarting the server.
+Invalid or unavailable persisted settings bypass compression. This advertises extension
+code and policy, not transform-service health or release qualification.
+
 Native function-result injection follows [the separate opt-in control contract](transports/streaming-health.md#experimental-native-function-result-injection); this surface does not infer upstream support or alter its defaults.
 
 Native steering follows [the shared WebSocket contract](transports/streaming-health.md#experimental-native-mid-turn-steering); this surface's defaults remain unchanged.
